{"nodes": [{"id": "mobile_html", "label": "mobile.html", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "mobile.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_rationale_simplification", "label": "mobile.html deliberate simplifications", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "mobile.html", "source_location": "lines 14-33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mobile.html is the static-Supabase 1:1 replacement for legacy Mobile.html (single-machine-per-screen phone UI). Simplifications matching duc-dashboard.html decisions: (1) dropped the Apps-Script-served PWA manifest (?asset=manifest) since this is a real static file on GitHub Pages \u2014 theme-color/apple-* meta tags suffice for 'Add to Home Screen'; (2) QR label printing now points TEM_PRINT_URL at intem.html instead of the old Apps Script flow; (3) dropped ensurePersonnelInMaster_ since there is no longer a master-data write path (master_employees is managed separately) \u2014 hand-typed names still save as free text, just lose next-time autosuggest; (4) machine/product/personnel/mold dropdowns now read directly from master_machines/master_products/master_employees/duc_shot_khuon (already migrated) instead of calling an api_bootstrap RPC. Also fixed an oversized root font-size (was hardcoded 48px, ~3x normal reading size) causing overflow on real phones \u2014 reverted to a clamp(15px,4vw,17px) browser-normal base."}, {"id": "mobile_bootstrap_equiv", "label": "loadMasterData() (mobile)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "mobile.html", "source_location": "line 484", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile_loadshiftstate", "label": "loadShiftState() (mobile)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "mobile.html", "source_location": "line 742", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "mobile